<title>POLAND: KGHM STARTS TRADE 11.9 PCT ABOVE ISSUE.</title>
<headline>KGHM STARTS TRADE 11.9 PCT ABOVE ISSUE.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish coppper firm KGHM Polska Miedz SA started trading on the main floor of the Warsaw Stock Exchange at 23.5 zlotys, 11.9 percent above its institutional- investor public-offering price of 21 zlotys.</p>
<p>The 14-million-share institutional-investor tranche of KGHM's public offering last week saw a 22-percent orders reduction, the 16-million-share retail tranche at 19 zlotys a 62-percent orders reduction.</p>
<p>Thursday's opening came slightly above analysts' predictions centering around 21 zlotys.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
